/** @mainpage Qore VSS Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section vssintro Introduction to the VSS Module

    The %VssLoader module provides support for the
    <a href="https://covesa.github.io/vehicle_signal_specification/">COVESA Vehicle Signal Specification (VSS)</a>,
    the industry-standard data model for vehicle signals.

    This module is released under the MIT license (see \ref COPYING.MIT "COPYING.MIT"
    for details).

    To use this module, use \c "%requires VssLoader" in your code.

    All the public symbols in the module are defined in the VssLoader namespace.

    @section vssmodules User Modules

    The following user modules are provided with this module:
    - @ref VssLoader "VssLoader": Core VSS loading, parsing, and validation functionality
    - @ref VssDataProvider "VssDataProvider": DataProvider integration for browsable VSS catalog
    - @ref VssDataProcessors "VssDataProcessors": Pipeline data processors for telemetry normalization

    @section vsscapabilities Capabilities

    - Native \c .vspec file parsing with \c #include directive resolution
    - Instance expansion (e.g. \c "Row[1,4]" to concrete paths)
    - Overlay merging (attribute override, path addition/deletion)
    - Pre-exported VSS JSON/YAML loading
    - Data validation against VSS catalogs (type, range, enum checks)
    - Extensible unit conversion (factor/offset model)
    - DataProvider browsable tree navigation
    - Pipeline processors: normalize, validate, convert, enrich

    @section vssexamples Examples

    @par Loading a VSS tree from a pre-exported file
    @code{.py}
%requires VssLoader

VssTree tree("/path/to/vss_v6.yaml");
printf("VSS tree has %d nodes\n", tree.size());
printf("Vehicle.Speed: %y\n", tree.getNode("Vehicle.Speed"));
    @endcode

    @par Parsing native .vspec files
    @code{.py}
%requires VssLoader

VssVspecParser parser("/path/to/vspec/dir");
hash<string, hash<VssNode>> nodes = parser.parseFile("Vehicle.vspec");

# expand instances
nodes = VssInstanceExpander::expandAll(nodes);

VssTree tree(nodes, "6.0");
    @endcode

    @par Validating signal data
    @code{.py}
%requires VssLoader

VssTree tree("/path/to/vss_v6.yaml");
VssValidator validator(tree);

list<hash<VssValidationError>> errors = validator.validateRecord({
    "Vehicle.Speed": 120.5,
    "Vehicle.Cabin.Door.Row1.DriverSide.IsOpen": True,
});
    @endcode

    @par Unit conversion
    @code{.py}
%requires VssLoader

VssUnitConverter converter();
float speed_ms = converter.convert(100.0, "km/h", "m/s");
    @endcode

    @section vssreleasenotes Release Notes

    @subsection vss_1_0 VssLoader 1.0
    - initial release
    - native \c .vspec file parsing with \c #include resolution
    - instance expansion and overlay merging
    - pre-exported VSS JSON/YAML loading
    - data validation (type, range, enum, unknown path)
    - unit conversion with factor/offset model
    - DataProvider integration with browsable VSS catalog
    - pipeline data processors (normalize, validate, convert, enrich)
*/
